 "Aaron Burr's treason trial and the Underwood in the jury pool": {
  "from": "The older Robards: a lot at the falls of the James, 6,000 acres in Kentucky, and Andrew Jackson's rival",
  "start": "**The uncle on Aaron Burr",
  "end": "*Sources:",
  "intro": "In 1807 the former vice president **Aaron Burr** stood trial at Richmond for treason, accused of plotting to carve an empire out of the western territories. Chief Justice John Marshall presided, and on 1 September the jury found him not guilty; a second trial on a lesser charge followed that month. Picking jurors who hadn't already made up their minds was nearly impossible, because the whole country had been reading about the plot for a year. One of the men called was very likely the brother of Kristin's 6th great-grandmother **Hannah Underwood**. (Burr turns up in family lore too: Marion County, Kentucky tradition says he once stopped at Daniel Everhart's house near Lebanon, though that's a legend, not a record.)",
